 patch face often refers to merfolk and  life under the sea in his songs and  riddles are they the ramblings of a man  whose wits had long been lost or are  they Stroud at truths under the sea men  marry fishes hatch face did a little  dance step jingling his bells they do  they do they do if it's true that patch  face gave his seed to a Merlin in the  song he sings here seems to fit this  would also parallel another legend and a  saga by some fire The Legend of the  night's king who gave his seed to a  woman that was pale and cold as ice and  with his seed he gave her his soul he  was bound to her for 13 years until  Jorma and the king of winter brought an  end to it could patch face half as well  given his soul to the Merlin if Merlin's  exists and patch face is bound to them  then what could be his goal take a  closer look at his riddles and songs and  you will find that it seems that he  desires to return to the sea not only to  return to the sea but to bring the  princess Shireen with him  I will lead it his bells rang merrily we  will march into the sea and out again  under the ways we will ride seahorses  and mermaids will blow seashells to  announce our coming oh oh oh away away  The Fool sing come with me beneath the  sea away away away he took the little  princess by one hand and drew her from  the room skipping but what use could the  Merlin's have for princess Shireen  throughout Westeros they're legends of  being is called squishers squishers are  scaled and fishy-smelling humanoids with  webbed hands and feet and teeth as sharp  as needles they are said to come by  night and steal children the girls they  keep to breed with the boys they are set  to eat on toad Isle of Essos there are a  race of people who claim to have been  descended from some humanoid fish  creature the people have webbed hands  and webbed feet and disturbingly  fish-like faces they worship an idol  made from black stone that's also said  to have been built by the creatures long  gone the creatures that they describe as  their ancestors sing very similar to  some of the other descriptions of sea  folk so there is evidence that these  so-called squishers do and have bred  with humans that means that the idea  that pache face gave his seed to a  merlin may not be as dubious as it  sounds it may also have other  implications just about everything we  know about the Merlin's and the  squishers is based on hearsay and legend  we have two independent sources that  tell us one thing however Merlin's breed  with humans and so do the so called  squishers it seems likely to me that it  is accurate to say that the legends of  the squishers and the merlynx refer to  the same beings the deep ones this idea  is backed up by the claims of maester  Theron of the Iron Islands they're on  argue that the legends of the merlynx  are actually in reference to the deep  ones these sea dwelling creatures are  known even in Lovecraftian lore from  which Martin has borrowed them from to  breed with humans this means that there  is a rather glaring possibility  that the purpose of Patch face is to  claim Shireen for the sea Steffon  Baratheon had no daughters only sons  three sons Stannis windley and Robert if  Stannis died  Shireen will be the rightful heir to the  Seven Kingdoms I have made several  connections between multiple artifacts  of Blackstone throughout the world and  the deep ones it seems that they  inhabited the world long before men ever  did it is claimed by some that these  creatures were destroyed by the first  men this seems unlikely to me however  there is evidence of conflicts between  mankind and these creatures the maze  makers of Laura were said to have been  destroyed by foes that came from the sea  the high tower of Old Town sits upon a  black stone that's more ancient in the  town itself the Isle it rests upon is  named battle Isle the reason for the  name is lost in time conflict between  men and the deep waters fits into the  themes of men versus nature that are  constant in our story while the  artifacts of the deep ones remain they  have seemingly vanished I do not believe  it is likely that they are extinct  however much like the children of the  forest they simply have retreated into  their natural habitat to flee humanity  back into the sea they have gone  Shireen's purpose is to breed with them  to give them heirs with the blood of  kings so that they themselves could lay  claim to Westeros but this would all  have to wait until Shireen was old  enough which has to be the reason that  patch face has not made his move yet he  must wait until she is a woman and then  and only then would he be free to take  her with him back into the sea thank you  guys for watching make sure you like and  subscribe for more ideas of Ice and Fire
 

